 already at that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"time, so a remove-then-insert edit of one entry among ties silently changes the order of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entries that were never touched. And — unlike a position — the identity keeps addressing"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"this same entry across any other entry’s edit, so a caller never needs to re-resolve it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The edit can turn this entry into an exact duplicate of another one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"already at the same time — same time, pan position, and extras —"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the same combination "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorModel\/documentation\/IvorModel\/PanMap\/insert(time:pan:extras:)"},{"type":"text","text":" silently"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"collapses. When that happens, "},{"code":"entryID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" always keeps addressing the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"entry that was just updated; the "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"other","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", pre-existing entry is the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"one silently removed instead. That is the only choice consistent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"with the guarantee above: a caller invoking this method already"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds "},{"code":"entryID","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" and goes on using it afterward, so honoring “this"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"identity keeps addressing this same entry” means the entry it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"wasn’t referencing has to be the one that gives way, never 